dertaking, recorded in the GO, to submit only onboarded books; (ii) the daily check's unexplained-plan rule sharpened for this decision: ANY plan whose book is not onboarded — whatever its phase — is a NORMAL-OPS-ANOMALY on sight and a T-1 trigger evaluation the same day; (iii) the turn-on's validity is tied to the decision: if an unonboarded-book plan is ever observed, the turn-on gate's declaration path is void until Rowan dispositions it.
- **What E3 does not do**: it does not make the exposure zero, bounded per book, or technically detected before spend begins (detection is daily, after the fact, though the cap/quota bound the maximum one-day exposure). Those are the reasons it is the fallback, not the recommendation.

